WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.730
Sign in with your approved Google account.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:11.739
In Video Studio, search Douyin and select one to five references.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.614
Upload your own vertical video, thirty seconds to three minutes long.

00:00:17.614 --> 00:00:20.183
Add a project name and script, and

00:00:20.183 --> 00:00:23.507
confirm your permission to edit the footage.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:28.015
Choose your topic and content language.

00:00:28.015 --> 00:00:32.554
Describe your audience, tone, and brand rules.

00:00:32.554 --> 00:00:37.290
Set your AI spending limit, then build the plan.

00:00:37.967 --> 00:00:43.078
Read the reference analysis, then open Director Timeline.

00:00:43.078 --> 00:00:46.933
Check each suggestion against your footage.

00:00:46.933 --> 00:00:52.134
Approve useful changes, lock decisions, and save the plan.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.646
For a different approach, choose an

00:00:55.646 --> 00:00:59.712
unlocked decision and describe what should change.

00:00:59.712 --> 00:01:04.266
Review the AI alternative before replacing the decision.

00:01:04.266 --> 00:01:06.787
Your other choices stay intact.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:12.434
Render the approved plan and watch the master preview.

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:17.034
Check the picture, speech, and subtitles yourself.

00:01:17.034 --> 00:01:20.806
Changes to the plan require a new render.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:24.643
Open Platform versions to create Douyin,

00:01:24.643 --> 00:01:28.136
Instagram Reels, and YouTube Shorts exports.

00:01:28.136 --> 00:01:31.868
Review each version, then download the package.

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:34.806
Lumen does not publish automatically.

